# CeraLive RK3588 `edge` kernel — FORBIDDEN symbol manifest
#
# Checked against a REAL resolved `.config` by
# `lib/verify-kernel-config.sh --config <.config> --forbidden <this file>`.
#
# Entries are BARE symbol names. A symbol listed here must resolve to not-set,
# or be absent from the tree entirely — both mean the same thing to the build.
# `CONFIG_X=<value>` is refused as a usage error rather than reinterpreted: this
# manifest states "this must not be in the kernel", never "this particular value
# is the bad one".
#
# THREE CLASSES, and each one is here for a different reason.
#
# 1. FOREIGN SoC PLATFORMS. arm64 `defconfig` enables every platform
#    arch/arm64/Kconfig.platforms offers, and each drags in its own clock,
#    pinctrl, PHY, DMA, thermal, mailbox and media drivers. Disabling them in
#    rk3588-edge.fragment removed 624 modules that can never bind on this
#    silicon. This list is what keeps them out: a defconfig refresh that
#    re-enables one, or a fragment edit that drops a line, fails the build
#    instead of quietly restoring the weight.
#
#    CONFIG_ARCH_REALTEK IS NOT THE Wi-Fi ADAPTER — it is Realtek's RTD12xx SoC
#    platform. The Rock 5B+ RTL8852BE is CONFIG_RTW89_8852BE, which the required
#    manifest pins as present. Do not "fix" a Wi-Fi problem by removing this row.
#
# 2. TEST AND DEBUG SYMBOLS. Production `edge` must resolve every fault-injection
#    control OFF. The CeraLive test seam exists only under the separate opt-in
#    `edge-test` variant, whose debugfs knobs compile to nothing unless it is set;
#    KASAN and lockdep belong to that variant too. A production artifact that
#    carried any of them would be a different kernel from the one validated on
#    hardware.
#
# 2b. THE ISLAND'S NON-COMPILED MPP CLIENTS. A closed capability surface is a
#    contract, not a default: the island compiles three clients and every other
#    one is source-only behind `depends on BROKEN`. These rows put that gate in
#    the image, so lifting a `BROKEN` upstream of us cannot quietly add a fourth
#    client to a shipped kernel.
#
# 3. SYMBOLS THAT DO NOT EXIST AT THIS PIN. CONFIG_NFT_COUNTER is real in the
#    sense that the ruleset's `counter` statement is load-bearing, but v7.2
#    compiles nft_counter.o unconditionally into nf_tables-objs and has no such
#    symbol. Re-verified at v7.2: a tree-wide search across every Kconfig,
#    Kconfig.* and Makefile returns zero hits, and net/netfilter/Makefile still
#    builds nft_counter.o into nf_tables-objs next to nft_meta.o and
#    nft_chain_filter.o. It is listed so a future "obviously missing" addition to
#    the fragment is caught here with an explanation rather than as a bare
#    DROPPED.

# --- 1. foreign SoC platforms ---------------------------------------------
CONFIG_ARCH_ACTIONS
CONFIG_ARCH_AIROHA
CONFIG_ARCH_ALPINE
CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE
CONFIG_ARCH_ARTPEC
# ARCH_ASPEED is NEW AT v7.2 — the prompt was added to
# arch/arm64/Kconfig.platforms AND set `=y` in arm64 defconfig in the same
# release, so an un-refreshed fragment would have carried defconfig's own `=y`
# straight into an RK3588 kernel (plus ten symbols it drags in). It is the
# counterexample to the old "a platform upstream adds later is simply absent
# rather than silently re-enabled" claim: the stale-list failure mode is a
# MISSING row, not a leftover one. Re-enumerate this block at every base bump.
CONFIG_ARCH_ASPEED
CONFIG_ARCH_AXIADO
CONFIG_ARCH_BCM
CONFIG_ARCH_BCM2835
CONFIG_ARCH_BCMBCA
CONFIG_ARCH_BCM_IPROC
CONFIG_ARCH_BERLIN
CONFIG_ARCH_BITMAIN
CONFIG_ARCH_BLAIZE
CONFIG_ARCH_BRCMSTB
CONFIG_ARCH_BST
CONFIG_ARCH_CIX
CONFIG_ARCH_EXYNOS
CONFIG_ARCH_HISI
CONFIG_ARCH_INTEL_SOCFPGA
CONFIG_ARCH_K3
CONFIG_ARCH_KEEMBAY
CONFIG_ARCH_LAN969X
CONFIG_ARCH_LAYERSCAPE
CONFIG_ARCH_LG1K
CONFIG_ARCH_MA35
CONFIG_ARCH_MEDIATEK
CONFIG_ARCH_MESON
CONFIG_ARCH_MICROCHIP
CONFIG_ARCH_MMP
CONFIG_ARCH_MVEBU
CONFIG_ARCH_MXC
CONFIG_ARCH_NPCM
CONFIG_ARCH_NXP
CONFIG_ARCH_PENSANDO
CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM
CONFIG_ARCH_REALTEK
CONFIG_ARCH_RENESAS
CONFIG_ARCH_S32
CONFIG_ARCH_SEATTLE
CONFIG_ARCH_SOPHGO
CONFIG_ARCH_SPARX5
CONFIG_ARCH_SPRD
CONFIG_ARCH_STM32
CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI
CONFIG_ARCH_SYNQUACER
CONFIG_ARCH_TEGRA
CONFIG_ARCH_TESLA_FSD
CONFIG_ARCH_THUNDER
CONFIG_ARCH_THUNDER2
CONFIG_ARCH_UNIPHIER
CONFIG_ARCH_VEXPRESS
CONFIG_ARCH_VISCONTI
CONFIG_ARCH_XGENE
CONFIG_ARCH_ZYNQMP

# --- 2. test / debug / fault injection --------------------------------------
# THE THREE OLD CeraLive TEST SYMBOLS ARE GONE, ALL THREE OF THEM, AND THAT IS MORE
# THAN THE OBVIOUS ONE. `VIDEO_ROCKCHIP_RKVENC_CERALIVE_TEST`,
# `VIDEO_ROCKCHIP_HDMIRX_CERALIVE_TEST` and `DMABUF_HEAPS_CERALIVE_TEST` were all
# three declared by ONE patch — the retired `0013` instrumentation member — even
# though the code they gated lived across the rkvenc, hdmirx and dma-heap patches.
# So retiring `0013` took the hdmirx and dma-heap symbols with it even though `0017`
# and `0018` survive. Verified against the applied tree at this `patches_commit`:
# none of the three names appears in any Kconfig. The island's own seam replaces all
# three, and it carries the same contract — `depends on DEBUG_FS`, `default n`,
# compiles to nothing when off — so production `edge` must resolve it OFF.
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_CERALIVE_TEST
CONFIG_KASAN
CONFIG_KCSAN
CONFIG_UBSAN
CONFIG_PROVE_LOCKING
CONFIG_DEBUG_LOCK_ALLOC
CONFIG_LOCK_STAT
CONFIG_KUNIT
CONFIG_FAULT_INJECTION
# KMEMLEAK was in NEITHER list before this change, and it is the one debug switch
# whose cost is invisible in a symbol survey: it is a `bool` that arm64 defconfig
# leaves off, so nothing was wrong — but it allocates a metadata object per kernel
# allocation and would turn a production encode path into a scanner. This row is
# therefore NON-VACUOUS BY INTENT RATHER THAN BY MEASUREMENT: it also measured
# not-set against the PRE-change resolved config, so it guards a future addition to
# the debug fragment leaking into production, not a defect being removed today.
CONFIG_DEBUG_KMEMLEAK
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO

# --- 2b. MNH-23: the island's non-compiled MPP clients ----------------------
# The island compiles EXACTLY THREE MPP clients — RKVENC2, RKVDEC2, JPGDEC — and its
# own ANTI-PATTERNS forbid a fourth. Every other client is retained as source for
# provenance behind `depends on BROKEN`, which is deliberate fail-closed policy and
# not a statement about the code. `BROKEN` makes them unselectable today; this block
# is what makes a future edit that lifts one visible HERE, in the image that would
# ship it, instead of only in the island's own review. Two of them are load-bearing
# refusals rather than housekeeping: AV1DEC would advertise an AV1 decoder whose
# Verisilicon provider is intentionally absent, and JPGENC would contend with
# mainline Hantro for the JPEG-encode block.
#
# NOTE THE SPELLING: the JPEG encoder's symbol is ROCKCHIP_MPP_JPGENC. There is no
# `ROCKCHIP_MPP_RKJPEGE` — `RKJPEGE` is the block name in the Kconfig prompt text,
# and a forbidden row naming it would silently guard nothing while the real symbol
# went unguarded.
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_RKVDEC
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_RKVENC
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_VDPU1
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_VEPU1
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_VDPU2
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_VEPU2
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_VEPU22
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_IEP2
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_JPGENC
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_AV1DEC
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_VDPP
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_RKVENC2_DEVFREQ
CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_MPP_RKVDEC2_DEVFREQ

# --- 3. absent at the v7.2 pin ----------------------------------------------
CONFIG_NFT_COUNTER
